****
Hydrogen alpha at 6563&Aring; is the strongest of the Balmer series, but beta, gamma and delta are also obvious lines in the spectrum. 
It is epsilon where hydrogen is no longer obvious, metal lines overwhelm the increasingly weak signal, and maybe the chromosphere 
pokes out at the disk edge to indicate that there is more there than meets the eye. 

In case of the epsilon line, it is a mere bump in the Calcium H valley. In comparison with the surrounding "continuum", 
it shows decreased contrast for the plages, prominences, and the darkest and densest of filaments show up, and of course flares.

The full hydrogen signal is still there though, as we'll see in the next image, it is just overwhelmed by the metal signal providing its baseline.
